From dd45c000073362c1921b4cc8191fa99ed6ce0ab4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:22:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/24] Lift a quarantine only on that mapping's own new
 backing

Three holes in the quarantine, each with its regression:

A partner's release lifted the other side. When the stale mapping's new
surfaces were unmapped, their pages went back to the kernel and the
stale one, left without partners, was lifted and its frame written
there: the corruption reopened. A partner's release now only updates the
record; each mapping lifts on its own lifecycle alone.

A MAP notification lifted outright, though it can trail the resolve that
already adopted the stale table and keep the same generation. A MAP, or a
new MappingInternal, now only arms the lift; the resolve that adopts a
table other than the one quarantined completes it, and the same table
re-announced lifts nothing. A delete that only condemns the table no
longer lifts either, since a reprieve re-reads it. Page proofs now carry a
write epoch that a revocation moves, so a proof minted before a quarantine
never covers again, whatever happens to the generation.

A store that discovered the collision itself, in the resolve its write
runs, returned false and the payment called the frame lost and copied out.
It now defers: the frame goes back to the ledger at its generation, its
resident keeps the only copy, and nothing is stamped as written.

